Rokan Terminal — judge sandbox

This is a throttled Linux container (1/4 vCPU, 1 GiB) that lives for 30 minutes.
You are `judge` (no sudo). It holds no API key and no secret, and its disk is wiped when it ends.
Outbound network access is open — the isolation here is that there is nothing to steal and nothing to spend.

Try:
  ls; git --version; python3 --version
  echo hello_judge

Then ask your agent (ChatGPT desktop with GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra, or Chrome 149+ with WebMCP)
to propose a command, press Enter, and forge what you just did into a tool.

`rokan do "<question> at <site>"` replays a verified, seeded operation with zero model calls (⚡) — 52 seeded
operations across 49 hosts; see SKILL.md here. Anything unseeded plans for real through a capped model proxy
(read-only task classes; the key never enters this container) and then replays at ⚡ next time.
